Z||000000||GT Bastard||09-25-2000||04:23 PM||||Lately I seem to have developed an exhaust leak.  I took a look at my headers and noticed 2 or 3 small leaks that have developed around the welds.  These headers are only a couple thousand miles old(1FST2M6 actually bought and installed them.)  The motor is going to be removed very soon, but I would assume that you can't weld them with the Jet-Hot coating on them.  So how does a person go about fixing this sort of thing?  Ruin the coating and weld them?  Has anybody else had a problem with the quality of Chris Wests headers?  <P>P.S. -- SH!T<P><BR>||||reg||13
Z||000001||88formula||09-25-2000||05:17 PM||||Call Chist West about the headers and see what he says first. Tell him if he does not fix them than you will tell everyone on this forum with 1400 members what happened. For $600 you should have no problems with those headers especially when you went through the trouble of having them coated.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||09-25-2000||07:47 PM||||I think you might have a better time dealing with Chris if you show him some respect and not try to threaten him with slamming him on the net. To my knowledge, Chris is a reputable guy providing reputable goods and services.  Perhaps it may have been more appropriate to take up this quality control issue with Chris via a phone call or private email rather then trashing him on the forum. Kinda took away your last resort, didn't ya?||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT Bastard||09-26-2000||08:37 AM||||I don't want to give Chris a bad reputation or anything, I'm just trying to solve my problem.  Any other ideas?  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||09-26-2000||08:59 AM||||i all ready said somthing similar to him about how they were put together... when you take them off look down the EGR tube... we had to re weld it after he already did.. had to do the same to the front set of tubes @ the block... only way to fix it... grind off the WAY -SPENSIVE finish and weld it...  <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A>    i really hope they help on a bigger motor.. cause they didn't do much to the 2.8... it made more HP at 6200-6500... uum factory redlines at 6... humm... chris is a good guy wioth nice stuff.. but these ones didn't turn out so great... <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-26-2000).]||||reg||1
